### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?

I don't think vim supports treesitter.nvim

### Operating system/version

Linux 5.16.16-artix1-1

### Terminal name/version

st 0.8.5

### $TERM environment variable

st-256color

### Installation

Artix repos

### How to reproduce the issue

1. Open a C file with treesitter.nvim.
2. Write into it :
```
#include <stdio.h>

struct LinkedList {
	char info[50];
	struct LinkedList *next;
};

int main() {
	struct LinkedList head = {"heeyyyyyy", NULL};
	head.next = &head;

	puts(head.next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next-next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next-next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next-next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->info);
}
```
3. Observe neovim segfaulting

### Expected behavior

NeoVim not segfaulting.

### Actual behavior

NeoVim segfaulting with `Thread 1 "v" received signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault. 0x00007ffff7eed03d in ts_query_cursor_next_capture () from /usr/lib/libtree-sitter.so.0`.
